    <bpmn:process id="W_W294" name="W294. Unit of Measure (UOM) Master &amp; Conversion Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Introduction of new UOM requirements (e.g., new product line sold by a different measure), conversion factor correction, or new supplier using a different purchasing UOM
Frequency: ~5–10 new UOM requests/month; ~2–3 conversion factor reviews/quarter
Volume: ~60 active UOM codes; ~150 conversion factors; ~5–10 new requests/month
Owner: Master Data Manager
Participants: Category Manager, Supply Chain Planner, Pricing Analyst, Master Data Analyst
Source: workflow W294 — Unit of Measure (UOM) Master &amp; Conversion Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W294_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W294_Lane1" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W294_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W294_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W294_Lane2" name="Master Data Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W294_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W294_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W294_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W294_Lane3" name="Master Data Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W294_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W294_Lane4" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W294_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W294_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W294_Start6" name="Introduction of new UOM requirements (e.g., new product line sold by a different…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W294_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W294_Task7" name="UOM Request">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: UOM Request: Category Manager or Supply Chain Planner requests a new UOM code or conversion factor (e.g., a new tile vendor sells by square meter but inventory is tracked by piece). Request specifies: base UOM, alternate UOM, conversion factor, and affected SKUs.
Responsible (R): Category Manager / Supply Chain Planner
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W294_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W294_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W294_Task8" name="Conversion Validation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Conversion Validation: Master Data Analyst validates the conversion factor mathematically and physically. For hardware retail, critical conversions include: board feet ↔ cubic meters, pieces ↔ square meters (tiles), meters ↔ feet (wire/pipes), kilograms ↔ pieces (nails/bolts). Analyst cross-references vendor packing lists and physical measurements.
Responsible (R): Master Data Analyst
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W294_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W294_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W294_Task9" name="Impact Assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Impact Assessment: System simulates the impact of the new/changed conversion factor on: (a) inventory valuation (WAC recalculation), (b) pricing (per-unit price consistency), and (c) replenishment (order quantity computation). Pricing Analyst reviews pricing impact.
Responsible (R): Master Data Analyst / Pricing Analyst
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W294_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W294_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W294_Task10" name="Approval &amp; Configuration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Approval &amp; Configuration: Master Data Manager approves the UOM/conversion. IT ERP Administrator configures the UOM in the ERP, linking it to the relevant item records and ensuring catch-weight flags are set correctly (W5B.2, W3B.3).
Responsible (R): Master Data Manager / IT ERP Administrator
Accountable (A): Master Data Manager
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W294_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W294_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W294_Task11" name="Downstream Sync">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Downstream Sync: New UOM/conversion is synced to POS (for selling), WMS (for receiving/putaway), ecommerce (for online display), and procurement (for PO creation).
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W294_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W294_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W294_Task12" name="Periodic Conversion Audit">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Periodic Conversion Audit: Quarterly, Master Data Analyst runs a conversion accuracy audit, comparing system conversion factors against actual physical measurements for high-volume catch-weight items (lumber, wire, tiles). Discrepancies trigger correction requests.
Responsible (R): Master Data Analyst
Accountable (A): Master Data Manager
Duration: 2 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W294_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W294_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W294_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W294_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W294_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-52 (ensure UOM conversion accuracy.) | - operational: quarterly conversion-accuracy audit against physical measurement
Owner: Master Data Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W294_Assoc15" sourceRef="W294_Annotation14" targetRef="W294_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W294_Flow16" sourceRef="W294_Start6" targetRef="W294_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W294_Flow17" sourceRef="W294_Task7" targetRef="W294_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W294_Flow18" sourceRef="W294_Task8" targetRef="W294_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W294_Flow19" sourceRef="W294_Task9" targetRef="W294_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W294_Flow20" sourceRef="W294_Task10" targetRef="W294_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W294_Flow21" sourceRef="W294_Task11" targetRef="W294_Task12" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W294_Flow22" sourceRef="W294_Task12" targetRef="W294_End13" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W294_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W294_plane" bpmnElement="W_W294">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W294_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W294_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1580" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W294_Lane2_di" bpmnElement="W294_Lane2" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="250" width="1580" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W294_Lane3_di" bpmnElement="W294_Lane3" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="420" width="1580" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W294_Lane4_di" bpmnElement="W294_Lane4" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="590" width="1580" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W294_Task7_di" bpmnElement="W294_Task7"><dc:Bounds x="400" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W294_Task8_di" bpmnElement="W294_Task8"><dc:Bounds x="610" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W294_Task9_di" bpmnElement="W294_Task9"><dc:Bounds x="820" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W294_Task10_di" bpmnElement="W294_Task10"><dc:Bounds x="1030" y="465" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W294_Task11_di" bpmnElement="W294_Task11"><dc:Bounds x="1240" y="635" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W294_Task12_di" bpmnElement="W294_Task12"><dc:Bounds x="1450" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W294_Start6_di" bpmnElement="W294_Start6"><dc:Bounds x="290" y="147" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W294_End13_di" bpmnElement="W294_End13"><dc:Bounds x="1680" y="657" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W294_Annotation14_di" bpmnElement="W294_Annotation14"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="800" width="360" height="60" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W294_Flow16_di" bpmnElement="W294_Flow16"><di:waypoint x="326" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="400" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W294_Flow17_di" bpmnElement="W294_Flow17"><di:waypoint x="580" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="610" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W294_Flow18_di" bpmnElement="W294_Flow18"><di:waypoint x="790" y="335" /><di:waypoint x="820" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W294_Flow19_di" bpmnElement="W294_Flow19"><di:waypoint x="1000" y="335" /><di:waypoint x="1030" y="505" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W294_Flow20_di" bpmnElement="W294_Flow20"><di:waypoint x="1210" y="505" /><di:waypoint x="1240" y="675" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W294_Flow21_di" bpmnElement="W294_Flow21"><di:waypoint x="1420" y="675" /><di:waypoint x="1450" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W294_Flow22_di" bpmnElement="W294_Flow22"><di:waypoint x="1630" y="335" /><di:waypoint x="1680" y="675" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W294_Assoc15_di" bpmnElement="W294_Assoc15"><di:waypoint x="340" y="800" /><di:waypoint x="308" y="183" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W295" name="W295. Payment Terms &amp; Settlement Rule Master Governance" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: New vendor/customer onboarding requiring payment terms, renegotiation of existing terms, or internal policy change to settlement rules
Frequency: ~20–30 new term assignments/month (linked to vendor/customer onboarding); ~2–3 policy changes/year
Volume: ~50 active payment term codes; ~1,000 vendor term assignments; ~5,400 B2B customer term assignments (5,200 trade + 200 corporate; non-default terms flagged for review)
Owner: Finance Controller
Participants: AP Supervisor, AR Manager, Category Manager (for vendor terms), Sales Manager (for customer terms), Master Data Analyst
Source: workflow W295 — Payment Terms &amp; Settlement Rule Master Governance</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W295_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W295_Lane1" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W295_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W295_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W295_Lane2" name="Finance Controller">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W295_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W295_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W295_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W295_Lane3" name="Master Data Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W295_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W295_Lane4" name="AP Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W295_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W295_Lane5" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W295_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W295_End15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W295_Start7" name="New vendor/customer onboarding requiring payment terms, renegotiation of existing terms…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W295_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W295_Task8" name="Terms Request">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Terms Request: During vendor onboarding (W36) or customer credit setup (W24), the requesting party proposes payment terms. Category Manager or Sales Manager submits the proposed terms with justification (e.g., &quot;Net 60 requested by top-10 vendor due to 45-day manufacturing lead time&quot;).
Responsible (R): Category Manager / Sales Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W295_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W295_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W295_Task9" name="Cash Flow Impact Analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Cash Flow Impact Analysis: Finance Controller analyzes the proposed terms against current cash flow projections (W233). System calculates the projected DSO (Days Sales Outstanding) or DPO (Days Payable Outstanding) impact of the new terms.
Responsible (R): Finance Controller
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W295_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W295_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W295_Task10" name="Approval">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Approval: Finance Controller approves standard terms (Net 30, Net 60, LC at Sight). Non-standard or extended terms (Net 90+, deferred payment) require CFO approval.
Responsible (R): Finance Controller / CFO
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W295_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W295_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W295_Task11" name="System Configuration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: System Configuration: Master Data Analyst configures the payment term in the ERP, specifying: base term (days), discount structure (e.g., 2/10 Net 30 = 2% discount if paid within 10 days), settlement method (bank transfer, LC, check, e-wallet), and default GL cash discount account. Links the term to the vendor/customer master record.
Responsible (R): Master Data Analyst
Accountable (A): Finance Controller
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W295_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W295_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W295_Task12" name="Early Payment Discount Governance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Early Payment Discount Governance: For terms with early payment discounts, AP Supervisor configures the discount capture rules in the AP module. System auto-calculates discount eligibility on the payment proposal run and flags invoices where paying early maximizes discount capture.
Responsible (R): AP Supervisor
Accountable (A): Finance Controller
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W295_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W295_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W295_Task13" name="Periodic Terms Review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Periodic Terms Review: Annually, Finance Controller reviews all active payment terms against industry benchmarks and company working capital targets. Terms that deviate significantly (e.g., vendor on Net 90 when industry standard is Net 30) are flagged for renegotiation.
Responsible (R): Finance Controller
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 4 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W295_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W295_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W295_Task14" name="Audit Trail">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Audit Trail: All changes to payment terms on vendor/customer records are logged with timestamp, old value, new value, and approver. Bank detail changes on vendor records trigger the 48-hour cooling-off period (W287 Step 5).
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W295_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W295_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W295_End15" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W295_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W295_Annotation16">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-329 (ensure controlled execution — Financial &amp; Operational Masters (PA-29.2).) | - operational: Finance Controller review and approval gate
Owner: Finance Controller</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W295_Assoc17" sourceRef="W295_Annotation16" targetRef="W295_Start7" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W295_Flow18" sourceRef="W295_Start7" targetRef="W295_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W295_Flow19" sourceRef="W295_Task8" targetRef="W295_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W295_Flow20" sourceRef="W295_Task9" targetRef="W295_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W295_Flow21" sourceRef="W295_Task10" targetRef="W295_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W295_Flow22" sourceRef="W295_Task11" targetRef="W295_Task12" />
