    <bpmn:process id="W_W305" name="W305. Intercompany Transfer Pricing Rule Master Governance" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: New IC service/goods flow establishment, annual transfer pricing review, regulatory rate change, or new legal entity creation
Frequency: Annual comprehensive review; ad-hoc for new IC flows (2–3/year)
Volume: ~15–20 active IC pricing rules across 5 entities and ~10 entity-pair transaction types
Owner: Corporate Controller
Participants: CFO, VP Supply Chain, COO, Tax Manager, IT ERP Administrator
Source: workflow W305 — Intercompany Transfer Pricing Rule Master Governance</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W305_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W305_Lane1" name="Corporate Controller">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W305_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W305_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W305_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W305_Lane2" name="Tax Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W305_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W305_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W305_Lane3" name="IT ERP Administrator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W305_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W305_Lane4" name="CFO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W305_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W305_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W305_Start6" name="New IC service/goods flow establishment, annual transfer pricing review, regulatory rate…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W305_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W305_Task7" name="IC Flow Identification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: IC Flow Identification: Corporate Controller identifies a new intercompany service or goods flow requiring a transfer pricing rule. Current IC flows include: (a) BuildRight Depot → Property Management: store/DC lease payments, (b) Depot → Logistics: warehousing/distribution fees, (c) Depot → Digital Commerce: per-order ecommerce fulfillment fees, (d) Depot → Logistics: inter-DC freight charges, (e) Holdings → all entities: management fees. For each flow, specifies the pricing method (cost-plus, comparable uncontrolled price, transactional net margin method).
Responsible (R): Corporate Controller
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W305_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W305_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W305_Task8" name="Arm&#x27;s-Length Pricing Calculation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Arm&#x27;s-Length Pricing Calculation: Tax Manager calculates the arm&#x27;s-length transfer price based on the selected method. For cost-plus: verifies the cost base (direct costs + allocated overhead) and applies the agreed markup percentage. For comparable uncontrolled price: benchmarks against market rates from third-party providers. Documents the calculation methodology and supporting data for BIR/transfer pricing documentation (W235).
Responsible (R): Tax Manager
Accountable (A): Corporate Controller
Duration: 2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W305_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W305_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W305_Task9" name="System Configuration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: System Configuration: IT ERP Administrator configures the IC pricing rule in the ERP, specifying: (a) source entity, (b) target entity, (c) transaction type (lease fee, distribution fee, fulfillment fee, management fee, freight), (d) pricing method, (e) rate/amount (per sqm, per order, per pallet, per kg, percentage of revenue), (f) cost center allocations for both entities, (g) GL accounts for IC AP/AR, (h) effective date. System auto-generates IC invoices based on these rules (W14).
Responsible (R): IT ERP Administrator
Accountable (A): Corporate Controller
Duration: 1 hour</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W305_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W305_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W305_Task10" name="Validation &amp; Testing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Validation &amp; Testing: Corporate Controller runs test IC transactions to verify: (a) correct IC invoice generation, (b) correct GL posting in both entities, (c) correct elimination during consolidation (W234), (d) correct cost center allocation. Tax Manager reviews the test results for arm&#x27;s-length compliance.
Responsible (R): Corporate Controller / Tax Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 1 hour</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W305_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W305_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W305_Task11" name="Approval">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Approval: CFO approves the IC pricing rule, confirming arm&#x27;s-length compliance and alignment with the company&#x27;s transfer pricing policy (W235). Rules above PHP 10M annual impact require Board approval.
Responsible (R): CFO
Accountable (A): Board (if &gt; PHP 10M)
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W305_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W305_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W305_Task12" name="Annual Transfer Pricing Review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Annual Transfer Pricing Review: Annually, Tax Manager and Corporate Controller review all active IC pricing rules: (a) verify rates against current market benchmarks, (b) update cost-plus calculations with current cost data, (c) confirm BIR compliance documentation is current, (d) assess whether any new IC flows need pricing rules. Updated rules are submitted for CFO approval.
Responsible (R): Tax Manager / Corporate Controller
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 8 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W305_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W305_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W305_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W305_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W305_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-329 (ensure controlled execution — Financial &amp; Operational Masters (PA-29.2).) | - operational: Corporate Controller review and approval gate
Owner: Corporate Controller</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W305_Assoc15" sourceRef="W305_Annotation14" targetRef="W305_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W305_Flow16" sourceRef="W305_Start6" targetRef="W305_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W305_Flow17" sourceRef="W305_Task7" targetRef="W305_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W305_Flow18" sourceRef="W305_Task8" targetRef="W305_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W305_Flow19" sourceRef="W305_Task9" targetRef="W305_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W305_Flow20" sourceRef="W305_Task10" targetRef="W305_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W305_Flow21" sourceRef="W305_Task11" targetRef="W305_Task12" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W305_Flow22" sourceRef="W305_Task12" targetRef="W305_End13" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W305_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W305_plane" bpmnElement="W_W305">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W305_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W305_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1580" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
